// D-Fend Reborn: the language strings of the program - the only place where
// they are defined. One line per string:
//
//   LANG_STRING(Name, Accessor, Number, "Section", "Key", "English text")
//
// - Name: constant NR_<Name> (e.g. for LanguageSetup->FileManagerText)
// - Accessor: LanguageSetup->Accessor() / SetAccessor() return / set the text
//   of the current language
// - Number: unique number of the string (the next free number of the section
//   group; tools/langstrings.py add finds it)
// - Section / Key: section and key in the language files (data/Lang/*.ini)
// - English text: the built-in default, used if a language file has no text
//   for the key; data/Lang/English.ini contains the same texts
//
// Variants: LANG_STRING_NO_ACCESSOR (no accessor functions),
// LANG_STRING_EXPR (default text is a C++ expression), LANG_STRING_INFO
// (language file information; the defaults are set in LanguageSetupUnit.cpp).
//
// To add a string: python3 tools/langstrings.py add <Section> <Key> <Name> "English" ["German"]
// (adds the line here and the texts to English.ini / German.ini);
// python3 tools/langstrings.py check verifies table and language files.
//
// This file is included several times with different definitions of the
// macros (LanguageSetupUnit.h: constants and accessors,
// LanguageSetupStrings.cpp: default texts); no include guard.


